  {
    "id": "bhagavad-gita_15_1",
    "text_slug": "bhagavad-gita",
    "chapter": 15,
    "verse": 1,
    "original": "श्रीभगवानुवाच |\nऊर्ध्वमूलमधःशाखमश्वत्थं प्राहुरव्ययम् |\nछन्दांसि यस्य पर्णानि यस्तं वेद स वेदवित् ||१५-१||",
    "transliteration": "śrībhagavānuvāca .\nūrdhvamūlamadhaḥśākhamaśvatthaṃ prāhuravyayam .\nchandāṃsi yasya parṇāni yastaṃ veda sa vedavit ||15-1||",
    "meaning": "15.1 The Blessed Lord said  They (the wise) speak of the indestructible peepul tree having its root above and branches below, whose leaves are the metres or hymns: he who knows it is a knower of the Vedas.",
