  {
    "id": "bhagavad-gita_15_2",
    "text_slug": "bhagavad-gita",
    "chapter": 15,
    "verse": 2,
    "original": "अधश्चोर्ध्वं प्रसृतास्तस्य शाखा\nगुणप्रवृद्धा विषयप्रवालाः |\nअधश्च मूलान्यनुसन्ततानि\nकर्मानुबन्धीनि मनुष्यलोके ||१५-२||",
    "transliteration": "adhaścordhvaṃ prasṛtāstasya śākhā guṇapravṛddhā viṣayapravālāḥ .\nadhaśca mūlānyanusantatāni karmānubandhīni manuṣyaloke ||15-2||",
    "meaning": "15.2 Below and above spread its branches, nourished by the Gunas; sense-objects are its buds; and below, in the world of men, stretch forth the roots, originating action.",
