  {
    "id": "bhagavad-gita_15_5",
    "text_slug": "bhagavad-gita",
    "chapter": 15,
    "verse": 5,
    "original": "निर्मानमोहा जितसङ्गदोषा\nअध्यात्मनित्या विनिवृत्तकामाः |\nद्वन्द्वैर्विमुक्ताः सुखदुःखसंज्ञैर्-\nगच्छन्त्यमूढाः पदमव्ययं तत् ||१५-५||",
    "transliteration": "nirmānamohā jitasaṅgadoṣā adhyātmanityā vinivṛttakāmāḥ .\ndvandvairvimuktāḥ sukhaduḥkhasaṃjñaira- gacchantyamūḍhāḥ padamavyayaṃ tat ||15-5||",
    "meaning": "15.5 Free from pride and delusion, victorious over the evil of attachment, dwelling constantly in the Self, their desires having completely turned away, freed from the pairs of opposites known as pleasure and pain, the undeluded reach the eternal goal.",
