  {
    "id": "bhagavad-gita_15_12",
    "text_slug": "bhagavad-gita",
    "chapter": 15,
    "verse": 12,
    "original": "यदादित्यगतं तेजो जगद्भासयतेऽखिलम् |\nयच्चन्द्रमसि यच्चाग्नौ तत्तेजो विद्धि मामकम् ||१५-१२||",
    "transliteration": "yadādityagataṃ tejo jagadbhāsayate.akhilam .\nyaccandramasi yaccāgnau tattejo viddhi māmakam ||15-12||",
    "meaning": "15.12 That light which residing in the sun illumines the whole world, that which is in the moon and in the fire  know that light to be Mine.",
    "layers": [
      {
        "author": "iskcon",
        "lang": "en",
        "type": "commentary",
        "content": "[PLACEHOLDER: ISKCON Commentary]"
      },
